NODE_ENV=production
PORT=4210
POSTGRES_USER=compliance_swarm
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
POSTGRES_DB=compliance_swarm
POSTGRES_APP_PASSWORD=changeme-app
# Host `postgres` and port 5432 here are the container-network address of the postgres
# service, not a host port -- correct for both dev and production, and unaffected by the
# dev override's 5433 host publish. Only host-side tooling (see TEST_DATABASE_URL below)
# uses localhost:5433.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://compliance_swarm_app:changeme-app@postgres:5432/compliance_swarm
COOKIE_SECRET=changeme-to-a-long-random-string
TZ=Pacific/Honolulu

# Unset (or anything other than "true") in a real deployment. Gates every ProcessPass
# demo-identity route (POST /api/processpass/identify and friends) — with this off, there is
# no password-free way into any account. Only ever set to "true" for a rehearsal/demo
# environment seeded via `DEMO_MODE=true node scripts/seed-demo.js` — see
# docs/JEFF_LUDWIG_DEMO.md.
# DEMO_MODE=true

# Where the repo's static Process prototypes (agents/, shared/, config/, templates/ — siblings
# of server/, not under it) live on disk, so app.js can serve them at /agents, /shared, etc.
# Leave unset for a plain `npm start` from a git checkout, and leave unset in production too —
# both cases already resolve to the right place on their own (a bare checkout on disk, or the
# Docker image, which now bakes these four directories in at the matching path; see
# server/Dockerfile). This only exists as an escape hatch for a deployment layout that isn't
# either of those. docker-compose.dev.yml still sets it to /app, paired with read-only bind
# mounts of the same four directories, purely so editing them shows up without an image
# rebuild — that pairing is optional dev convenience, not a requirement.
# PROCESS_STATIC_ROOT=/app

# Real passkey (WebAuthn) sign-in — see server/src/routes/webauthn.js and
# services/identityProviders/PasskeyIdentityProvider.js. Both are origin-bound: a passkey
# registered against one rpID/origin pair will not verify against another. The defaults below
# (localhost / http://localhost:<PORT>) are correct for local dev only — browsers treat
# localhost as a secure context without TLS, which is what makes that work over plain http.
# A real deployment MUST set both to the actual public hostname it's reached at (e.g. behind
# the Cloudflare Tunnel — see app.js's trust proxy comment), or every passkey ceremony will
# fail to verify.
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=compliance-swarm.example.com
# WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=https://compliance-swarm.example.com

# Test runs only (never set in a deployed .env). Required by `npm test`, which has no
# DATABASE_URL fallback because production shares this database name.
#
# Port 5433 below is the DEV-ONLY host port -- it is not a general default. Postgres
# listens on 5433 only when the dev stack is brought up through the local override:
#
#   cd server && docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d postgres
#
# Host port 5432 belongs to the production Postgres container; never point a test run there.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://compliance_swarm_app:changeme-app@localhost:5433/compliance_swarm_test
